Rationale: The claim has two material parts: (1) the capture of the Japanese 20mm Cannon Blockhouse in the early stages of an engagement by American forces, and (2) the Battle of Manila being fought by American forces. The evidence supports that the Battle of Manila was fought by American and Philippine forces against Japanese troops. However, there is no reliable evidence identifying the engagement involving the capture of the Japanese 20mm Cannon Blockhouse, and the search for this information has returned insufficient results. Therefore, further investigation is needed to confirm the first part of the claim.
